      "card_ids": ["C16"],
      "claim": "The closest analogue (T-773, Morgan similarity 0.6714) showed good brain penetration and striatum-selective accumulation in a monkey PET study, directly demonstrating that this pyridazinone/phenylpyrazole scaffold can achieve meaningful CNS access after systemic administration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "A lower-similarity carboxylic acid analogue containing the same pyrazolylphenyl motif was a rat P-gp substrate with a CSF/unbound plasma ratio of 0.05, indicating that polar/acidic modifications can severely limit CNS exposure; however, this is less transferable because the query lacks the carboxylic acid and is structurally much closer to the brain-penetrant PET tracer.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The high-similarity direct monkey PET evidence for the THP analogue strongly supports meaningful CNS access for the query. The contradictory low-similarity carboxylic acid analogue is outweighed by the close structural match to a brain-penetrant tracer, and the query's replacement of THP with pyrazol-1-yl is not expected to abolish brain penetration.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct BBB/PK measurement exists for the exact query molecule; the closest evidence is a THP analogue with Morgan similarity 0.6714.",
    "The effect of replacing tetrahydropyran with pyrazol-1-yl on passive permeability and P-gp/Bcrp efflux is not directly measured."
  ],
